### F2. Reflection Directions

**✅ SPECIFICATION:**

```lisp
(deftype reflection-direction ()
  "Direction of reflection in meta-hierarchy.
   
   Values:
     :up - Move to higher meta-level (object → meta)
     :down - Move to lower meta-level (meta → object)
     :lateral - Stay at same level, different perspective
     :transcend - Jump multiple levels up
     :collapse - Jump multiple levels down
   
   Examples:
     Level 0 (object) --:up--> Level 1 (meta)
     Level 1 (meta) --:down--> Level 0 (object)
     Level 1 --:lateral--> Level 1 (different aspect)
     Level 0 --:transcend--> Level 5 (direct jump)
     Level 5 --:collapse--> Level 0 (direct jump)"
  
  '(member :up :down :lateral :transcend :collapse))

(defun reflect (evaluator expression direction &optional (levels 1))
  "Perform reflection in specified direction.
   
   Parameters:
     evaluator - The evaluator instance
     expression - Expression to reflect on
     direction - :up | :down | :lateral | :transcend | :collapse
     levels - Number of levels to move (for :transcend/:collapse)
   
   Returns: Reflected evaluation frame"
  
  (ecase direction
    (:up
     ;; Move up one meta-level
     (let ((current-level (evaluator-meta-level evaluator)))
       (setf (evaluator-meta-level evaluator) (1+ current-level))
       (call-reflection-hook evaluator expression 
                             :depth (1+ current-level)
                             :direction :up)))
    
    (:down
     ;; Move down one meta-level
     (let ((current-level (evaluator-meta-level evaluator)))
       (when (> current-level 0)
         (setf (evaluator-meta-level evaluator) (1- current-level)))
       (call-reflection-hook evaluator expression
                             :depth (1- current-level)
                             :direction :down)))
    
    (:lateral
     ;; Stay at same level, different perspective
     (call-reflection-hook evaluator expression
                           :depth (evaluator-meta-level evaluator)
                           :direction :lateral))
    
    (:transcend
     ;; Jump multiple levels up
     (let ((current-level (evaluator-meta-level evaluator)))
       (setf (evaluator-meta-level evaluator) (+ current-level levels))
       (call-reflection-hook evaluator expression
                             :depth (+ current-level levels)
                             :direction :transcend)))
    
    (:collapse
     ;; Jump multiple levels down
     (let ((current-level (evaluator-meta-level evaluator)))
       (setf (evaluator-meta-level evaluator) (max 0 (- current-level levels)))
       (call-reflection-hook evaluator expression
                             :depth (max 0 (- current-level levels))
                             :direction :collapse)))))
```

